Blackdrift: make Startpage the default search engine in every region.

Why: Focus picks its default engine from Mozilla's region-dependent search
configuration (android-components' bundled assets/search/list.json; the
Remote Settings search-config-v2 path is off by default through the Nimbus
remote-search-configuration flag), usually Google with Mozilla partner codes.
Blackdrift should not send searches under Mozilla's commercial codes. Startpage is
not in Mozilla's list, so a new BlackdriftSearchMigration wraps Focus's
SearchMigration (SearchMiddleware's migration hook): on the first engine load
after install it adds Startpage as a search engine (with suggestions) and
selects it as the user's default, once. This works for the bundled and the
remote configuration alike and does not edit Mozilla's engine list; users can
still pick any other engine. Only a one-line wiring change touches upstream
code (Components.kt).

Cut against: mozilla-firefox/firefox@6181e6b5f28a8fbae1d5c3ef6f6626b5a2180213 (Firefox 159.0.1).

